# Petrified Hamlet's trigger asks for a land card name as it resolves (CR 201.4a): Lightning Bolt is refused, Wasteland
# is taken and remembered by the Hamlet (CR 607.2d). From then on Wasteland's destroy ability can't be activated by
# either player, the Hamlet's controller included (CR 602.5), but its {T}: Add {C} still can, a mana ability
# (CR 605.1a). Strip Mine, not the chosen name, destroys the Hamlet (the control), and with the Hamlet gone Bot2's
# Wasteland destroys Bot1's.

[Bot1 Deck]
Wasteland
Petrified Hamlet
Island x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Wasteland
Strip Mine
Island x13

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Wasteland.Play
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Wasteland.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Petrified Hamlet.Play
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
! Bot1.Name(Lightning Bolt)
Bot1.Name(Wasteland)
? Bot1.Battlefield.Petrified Hamlet.ChosenName = Wasteland
! Bot1.Battlefield.Wasteland.Activate(Ability: Destroy)
Bot1.Battlefield.Wasteland.Activate(Ability: #1)
? Bot1.Mana = {C}
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
! Bot2.Battlefield.Wasteland.Activate(Ability: Destroy)
Bot2.Hand.Strip Mine.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Strip Mine.Activate(Bot1.Battlefield.Petrified Hamlet; Ability: Destroy)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
? Bot1.Graveyard = Petrified Hamlet
Bot2.Battlefield.Wasteland.Activate(Bot1.Battlefield.Wasteland; Ability: Destroy)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass

[Expect]
Turn = 4
Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 0
Bot1.Graveyard = Wasteland; Petrified Hamlet
Bot2.Graveyard = Wasteland; Strip Mine
